<!--
    Kurdish — Kurmanji, in Latin script.

    Which Kurdish is a real decision and it went this way for a specific reason:
    the readers here are drivers, and the drivers on this corridor are hired
    from carriers in Gaziantep, Şanlıurfa, Mardin and Şırnak, where Kurmanji in
    the Latin alphabet is what people read and write. Sorani, in Arabic script,
    is what Erbil reads — but Erbil is the consignee, and the consignee has the
    web page, which is already Arabic. A driver handed Sorani in a script they
    do not read would be worse served than by Turkish.

    So: values-ku is Kurmanji, left-to-right, and if Sorani is ever wanted for
    an Iraqi-hired driver it belongs in values-ckb with an RTL layout, not here.

    Numbers arrive already formatted with Latin digits, which suits this locale
    without further thought.

    The app_name is deliberately NOT translated — it is what a driver looks for
    in a launcher and what a dispatcher says down a phone.
-->
